+# Architecture: Takoboto-Class Dictionary UX & API Foundation (Phase 14.4F)
+
+## 1. Executive Summary
+
+Phase 14.4F exposes the core Japanese language intelligence ingested during Phases 14.3A–14.4E (206,749 dictionary records, 13,108 canonical kanji, radicals, KanjiVG stroke vectors, bidirectional lexical graph) via a responsive, accessible web experience and stable JSON APIs.
+
+The system mirrors the pedagogical depth of reference tools like Takoboto and Jisho while enforcing strict architectural boundaries:
+- **Zero Canonical Mutations**: Pure read-only presentation of canonical corpus records.
+- **CMS Editorial Overlay**: Transparent overlay for verified community translations and editorial fixes without corrupting upstream provenance.
+- **Deterministic AI Isolation**: Strict prohibition of ungrounded or speculative generative AI classifications.
+- **Mobile First & Responsive**: Dual-mode API response contracts supporting full desktop payloads and compact mobile cards.
+
+---
+
+## 2. System Topology & Architectural Layers
+
+```
+┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│                        Web Client / Mobile App                         │
+│   - /dictionary (Search & Discovery)                                   │
+│   - /dictionary/[id] (Rich Entry Detail)                               │
+│   - /kanji (Kanji Explorer & Filters)                                  │
+│   - /kanji/[character] (Takoboto-Class Kanji Detail & Mind Tree)       │
+└───────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
+                                    │ HTTP / REST
+┌───────────────────────────────────▼────────────────────────────────────┐
+│                       Next.js App Router Layer                         │
+│   - GET /api/dictionary (Search & Pagination)                          │
+│   - GET /api/dictionary/[id] (Entry Detail & Translations)             │
+│   - GET /api/kanji/[character] (Kanji Intelligence & SVGs)             │
+│   - GET /api/kanji/[character]/vocabulary (Lexical Graph Explorer)     │
+│   - GET /api/kanji/[character]/readings (Reading Taxonomy)             │
+│   - GET /api/kanji/[character]/components (Radicals & Constituents)    │
+└───────────────────┬────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────┘
+                    │                                │
+┌───────────────────▼──────────────┐  ┌──────────────▼───────────────────┐
+│        Dictionary Service        │  │     Kanji Lexical & Visual       │
+│  - Exact headword & reading      │  │  - KanjiLexicalGraphService      │
+│  - Romaji & English search       │  │  - KanjiVisualService (KanjiVG)  │
+│  - Multilingual overlay          │  │  - Mind Tree Assembly            │
+│  - Keigo classification          │  │  - Discrepancy Reconciliation    │
+└───────────────────┬──────────────┘  └──────────────┬───────────────────┘
+                    │                                │
+┌───────────────────▼────────────────────────────────▼───────────────────┐
+│                          Database Storage                              │
+│   - dictionary_entries (206,747 entries)                               │
+│   - kanji_entries (13,108 canonical kanji)                             │
+│   - kanji_radicals & kanji_composition                                 │
+│   - entity_translations (Verified Multilingual Translations)           │
+│   - data/kanjivg/*.svg (11,658 KanjiVG Vector Assets)                  │
+└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+
+---
+
+## 3. Search Engine & Resolution Pipeline
+
+The dictionary search endpoint (`/api/dictionary` and `/api/dictionary/search`) executes multi-strategy lexical matching:
+
+1. **Exact Headword Lookup**: Queries matching `headword = :query` are prioritized first with highest relevance rank.
+2. **Exact Reading Lookup**: Matches against `reading = :query` (Hiragana or Katakana).
+3. **Romaji Normalization**: Latin-character input is automatically converted to Kana candidates using Hepburn phonetics.
+4. **Kanji Substring Matching**: Single or multi-character kanji inputs match headwords containing those kanji (e.g. `水` matches `水`, `水道`, `水着`).
+5. **English Gloss / Full-Text Search**: Matches against English definitions using trigram or ILIKE substring queries.
+6. **JLPT Level & Common Word Filtering**: Enables scoping queries to `N5` through `N1` or common vocabulary (`common=true`).
+7. **Pagination**: Bounded `limit` (1..100, default 20) and `offset` (>= 0) parameter handling.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Entry Detail & Lexical Graph Integration
+
+When navigating to `/dictionary/[id]`:
+- **Kanji Decomposition**: The headword is parsed into constituent kanji. Each kanji is rendered as an interactive card displaying its primary English meaning, On/Kun readings, and a direct link to `/kanji/[char]`.
+- **Related Compound Vocabulary**: Bidirectional compound discovery through the lexical graph, surfacing compounds sharing constituent kanji.
+- **Multilingual Extensions**: Automatic lookup in `entity_translations`, returning human-verified translations in Spanish, French, German, or other supported locales.
+- **Keigo Extension Points**: Structured placeholder fields for honorific (*sonkeigo*), humble (*kenjougo*), and polite (*teineigo*) variants.
+- **Context Metadata**: Audio pronunciation tags, pitch accent indicators, and JLPT tier badges.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Performance & Security Invariants
+
+1. **Strict Input Sanitization**:
+   - `limit` parameter is capped at `100` max (enforced server-side). Negative limits clamp to default `20`.
+   - `offset` parameter rejects negative integers, clamping to `0`.
+   - SQL injection vectors and control characters are parameterized safely via Drizzle ORM and `pg` drivers.
+2. **CMS Security Boundary**:
+   - Learner code under `src/services/dictionary` and `src/services/knowledge` accesses published translations via the normalized view or `entity_translations` table without referencing draft/audit internals (`cms_content_items`, `cms_audit_log`).
+3. **Deterministic Graph Traversal**:
+   - In-memory graph nodes and runtime joins are deterministic; identical database state guarantees identical response digests across passes.
