+# Tatoeba Acquisition & Dry-Run Pipeline Contract
+
+**Phase**: 14.5A — Tatoeba Sentence Acquisition & Provenance Foundation  
+**Target Environment**: Isolated Local / CI Execution  
+**Database Writes**: STRICTLY FORBIDDEN (0 writes)  
+**Production Access**: STRICTLY FORBIDDEN (0 connections)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Pipeline Execution Flow
+
+```
+┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│             Raw Tatoeba Artifacts                      │
+│   data/tatoeba/sentences.tsv                           │
+│   data/tatoeba/links.tsv                               │
+│   data/tatoeba/tags.tsv                                │
+└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
+                           │
+┌──────────────────────────▼─────────────────────────────┐
+│          Step 1: Acquisition Verification              │
+│   - TatoebaAcquisitionManager.resolveSafePath()        │
+│   - SHA-256 Checksum Computation                       │
+│   - Compare with Acquisition Manifest                  │
+└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
+                           │
+┌──────────────────────────▼─────────────────────────────┐
+│          Step 2: Streaming Parse & Filter              │
+│   - TatoebaParser.parseSentenceLine()                  │
+│   - Filter: lang === "jpn"                             │
+│   - Index English & Target Translations                │
+└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
+                           │
+┌──────────────────────────▼─────────────────────────────┐
+│          Step 3: Normalization & Diagnostics           │
+│   - normalizeJapaneseText() (NFKC + Whitespace)        │
+│   - analyzeJapaneseScript() (Kanji, Kana, Digits)      │
+│   - Duplicate Text Mapping                             │
+└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
+                           │
+┌──────────────────────────▼─────────────────────────────┐
+│          Step 4: Quality Validation & Assembly         │
+│   - TatoebaValidator.validate()                        │
+│   - Assign status: valid | warning | rejected          │
+│   - Resolve Translation Links                          │
+│   - Generate Deterministic ID: es-tat-<id>             │
+│   - Stamp Provenance (sourceRef, CC-BY-2.0-FR)         │
+└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
+                           │
+┌──────────────────────────▼─────────────────────────────┐
+│          Step 5: Safety Guard & Reporting              │
+│   - Assert 0 Database Writes                           │
+│   - Compute Deterministic SHA-256 Digest               │
+│   - Emit TatoebaDryRunStats & Manifest                 │
+└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+
+---
+
+## 2. Invariant Rules
+
+1. **Database Safety Lock**:
+   If a persistence adapter is supplied or `dryRun: false` is configured, `TatoebaDryRunPipeline.execute()` throws `DatabaseSafetyViolationError` immediately.
+2. **Path Traversal Defense**:
+   Target files must resolve strictly within `data/tatoeba/`. Any attempt to access paths with `../` or root paths outside the repository root fails closed.
+3. **Fail-Closed Verification**:
+   If an artifact's computed SHA-256 deviates from the manifest by even one bit, processing halts with an explicit error.
+4. **Deterministic Processing Digest**:
+   Given identical raw input files and pipeline code:
+   $$\text{Digest}_1 = \text{Digest}_2$$
+   The SHA-256 digest is calculated over stable normalized outputs (`id`, `normalizedText`, `status`, `translationCount`), ensuring run-to-run reproducibility.
