+# Tatoeba Sentence Data Model & Relational Topology
+
+**Phase**: 14.5A — Tatoeba Sentence Acquisition & Provenance Foundation  
+**Schema Target**: `example_sentences` (and future enrichment overlays)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Domain Separation & Knowledge Classification
+
+NihongoBridge strictly separates six layers of knowledge:
+
+| Classification | Meaning & Scope in Sentence Architecture |
+|---|---|
+| **Upstream** | Raw, unmodified records exported directly from Tatoeba (`sentences.tsv`, `links.tsv`). |
+| **Canonical** | Formally ingested, validated sentences stored in `example_sentences` with immutable `sourceRef`. |
+| **Derived** | Deterministic relational edges extracted from sentence text (e.g. matched Kanji, matched dictionary words). |
+| **Editorial** | Verified human translations, pedagogical corrections, or curation overrides maintained in the CMS overlay. |
+| **Learner** | Student-specific data (SRS review states, bookmarks, test answers) stored in isolated learner tables. |
+| **AI** | Ephemeral, non-authoritative explanations or tutoring commentary. **Never canonical.** |
+
+---
+
+## 2. Upstream to Canonical Mapping
+
+```
+Upstream Tatoeba Record (sentences.tsv)
+  ├─ sentence_id: "1001"
+  ├─ lang: "jpn"
+  └─ text: "冷たい水を一杯飲みました。"
+       │
+       ▼ [Normalization & Validation]
+Canonical Example Sentence (example_sentences)
+  ├─ id: "es-tat-1001"
+  ├─ japanese: "冷たい水を一杯飲みました。"
+  ├─ reading: "つめたいみずをいっぱいのみました。"
+  ├─ english: "I drank a glass of cold water."
+  ├─ jlpt_level: "N5"
+  ├─ grammar_id: null
+  ├─ dictionary_entry_ids: ["de-mizu", "de-jmdict-1000010"]  [Derived]
+  ├─ kanji_characters: ["冷", "水", "一", "杯", "飲"]           [Derived]
+  ├─ tags: ["daily-life", "beverage", "jlpt:n5"]
+  └─ source_ref: "upstream:tatoeba:2024-07"
+```
+
+---
+
+## 3. Relational Topology & Future Linkage Contracts
+
+### 3.1 Kanji Linkage Contract
+- Deterministically extracted from sentence text:
+  $$\text{Kanji}(\text{Sentence}) = \{ c \in \text{Sentence} \mid c \in \text{CJK Unified Ideographs} \}$$
+- Every extracted character points directly to `kanji_entries.character`. No sentence-specific kanji copies are created.
+
+### 3.2 Dictionary Entry Linkage Contract
+- Uses `SentenceMatcher` trie/substring mapping to locate canonical dictionary headwords (`dictionary_entries.headword`).
+- Only verified dictionary entry IDs (`dictionary_entry_ids`) are stored.
+
+### 3.3 Grammar Pattern Linkage Contract
+- Identifies grammatical structures (e.g. `〜てから`, `〜なければならない`) matching `grammar_patterns.id`.
+
+### 3.4 Translation Linkage Topology
+- Preserves 1:N and N:1 translation mappings.
+- A Japanese sentence may link to multiple English translations (e.g. literal vs natural).
+- Multiple Japanese sentences (e.g. formal vs colloquial) may link to a single English concept.
