+# Tatoeba Sentence Model & Normalization Architecture (Phase 14.5B)
+
+## 1. Overview & Architectural Role
+
+Phase 14.5B establishes the intermediate sentence intelligence layer for Tatoeba Japanese example sentences in NihongoBridge. It bridges raw upstream exports (`upstream:tatoeba:2024-07`) with canonical knowledge graphs without mutating the production database.
+
+```
+┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│             Raw Tatoeba Exports (TSV)                  │
+│   sentences.tsv | links.tsv | tags.tsv                 │
+└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
+                           │
+┌──────────────────────────▼─────────────────────────────┐
+│          Normalization & Script Profiling              │
+│   - Unicode NFC canonical composition                  │
+│   - Control character removal                          │
+│   - Whitespace canonicalization                        │
+│   - Script profile (KANJI_KANA, KANA_ONLY, etc.)       │
+└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
+                           │
+┌──────────────────────────▼─────────────────────────────┐
+│          Validation & Quality Taxonomy                 │
+│   - ACCEPTED, ACCEPTED_WITH_WARNING, UNTRANSLATED      │
+│   - Pedagogical & orthographic warnings                │
+└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
+                           │
+┌──────────────────────────▼─────────────────────────────┐
+│          Canonical Relational Linkages                 │
+│   - Kanji Linkage (positional code points)             │
+│   - Dictionary Linkage (exact headword matches)        │
+│   - Translation Linkage (1:1, 1:N, N:1)                │
+│   - Derived JLPT Profile                               │
+└──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
+                           │
+┌──────────────────────────▼─────────────────────────────┐
+│          Deterministic Output & Provenance             │
+│   - es-tat-<upstreamId>                                │
+│   - Stable SHA-256 Digest ($Run_1 \equiv Run_2$)       │
+└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+
+---
+
+## 2. Sentence Normalization Contract
+
+1. **Original vs Normalized Text**: Both `originalText` (raw source) and `normalizedText` are preserved in the sentence contract.
+2. **Unicode NFC**: Employs canonical composition (NFC) to unify decomposed kana/diacritics while faithfully preserving Japanese full-width punctuation (`「」`, `、`, `。`, `！`, `？`), full-width numerals (`１５００円`), and kanji glyphs.
+3. **Control Character Elimination**: Strips hazardous non-printable ASCII control codes (0x00–0x1F, 0x7F).
+4. **Whitespace Handling**: Edge whitespace is trimmed, and consecutive internal spaces are collapsed.
+5. **Zero Semantic Alteration**: Grammatical structures, spelling, and vocabulary are never rewritten or corrected.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Script Profiling & Token Estimation
+
+Every sentence is classified into an orthographic script profile:
+- **`KANJI_KANA`**: Standard Japanese sentences combining kanji and kana (no Latin text).
+- **`KANA_ONLY`**: Sentences composed exclusively of hiragana/katakana and punctuation.
+- **`KANJI_LATIN_MIXED`**: Sentences containing kanji and Latin loanwords or acronyms (e.g. `Wi-Fi`, `PDF`).
+- **`KANA_LATIN_MIXED`**: Sentences containing kana and Latin characters without kanji.
+- **`OTHER`**: Sentences consisting primarily of digits, foreign characters, or symbols.
+
+Token count is estimated deterministically based on script transition boundaries (transitions between kanji, hiragana, katakana, Latin, and punctuation).
+
+---
+
+## 4. Quality Taxonomy & Warning Classification
+
+Sentences are categorized into 5 mutually exclusive statuses:
+- **`ACCEPTED`**: Structurally valid Japanese sentence with verified orthography and linked translation.
+- **`ACCEPTED_WITH_WARNING`**: Valid Japanese sentence exhibiting non-fatal pedagogical or orthographic anomalies.
+- **`UNTRANSLATED`**: Valid Japanese sentence that currently lacks a linked translation (`MISSING_TRANSLATION`).
+- **`RELATIONSHIP_ONLY`**: Non-Japanese sentence that serves strictly as a translation target node.
+- **`INVALID`**: Fatal structural failure (missing/invalid ID, empty text, or corrupted columns).
+
+### Warning Taxonomy
+| Code | Threshold / Trigger | Action |
+|---|---|---|
+| `EMPTY_TEXT` | Text length 0 | Fatal / Reject |
+| `SHORT_SENTENCE` | Character count < 3 | Flag for learner review |
+| `LONG_SENTENCE` | Character count > 120 | Flag for reading complexity |
+| `CONTROL_CHARACTER` | ASCII 0x00–0x1F detected | Stripped during normalization |
+| `REPLACEMENT_CHARACTER` | Unicode U+FFFD detected | Flag encoding issue |
+| `EXCESSIVE_SYMBOLS` | Non-linguistic symbols > 5 | Flag formatting noise |
+| `REPEATED_PUNCTUATION` | Punctuation runs $\ge 3$ | Flag informal text |
+| `SUSPICIOUS_MARKUP` | HTML/XML tags or unescaped entities | Flag for sanitization |
+| `UNUSUAL_UNICODE` | Private-use codepoints (U+E000–U+F8FF) | Flag non-standard glyphs |
+| `DUPLICATE_TEXT` | Same Japanese text in multiple IDs | Retain both; flag duplicate |
+| `MISSING_TRANSLATION` | Zero linked translations | Set status to `UNTRANSLATED` |
+| `UNKNOWN_KANJI_CHARACTER` | Kanji absent from `kanji_entries` | Flag as non-canonical |
+
+---
+
+## 5. Duplicate Policy
+
+1. **Upstream Duplicate IDs**: If the identical Tatoeba sentence ID appears multiple times in raw source files, it is rejected as a data integrity violation.
+2. **Duplicate Japanese Text**: If different upstream IDs contain identical Japanese sentences (e.g. `こんにちは。` under IDs 1076 and 1077), both records are preserved independently. This protects unique translation links, contributor histories, and submission timestamps. A non-fatal `DUPLICATE_TEXT` warning is attached.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Provenance & Attribution Contract
+
+Every normalized sentence generates a learner-facing `TatoebaAttributionInfo` contract:
+```ts
+{
+  sourceName: "Tatoeba",
+  sourceId: "upstream:tatoeba:2024-07",
+  sentenceId: "1001",
+  canonicalUrl: "https://tatoeba.org/sentences/show/1001",
+  license: "CC-BY-2.0-FR",
+  attributionStatement: "Tatoeba Project (tatoeba.org) contributors under Creative Commons BY 2.0 FR"
+}
+```
+Attribution metadata is never stripped or discarded during transformation.
