+# Tatoeba Sentence Provenance & Legal Compliance Specification
+
+**Phase**: 14.5A — Tatoeba Sentence Acquisition & Provenance Foundation  
+**Status**: APPROVED  
+**Author**: Lead Data-Architecture & ETL Engineer  
+**Canonical Source ID**: `upstream:tatoeba:2024-07`  
+**License**: Creative Commons Attribution 2.0 France (CC BY 2.0 FR)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Upstream Source Identity & Governance
+
+The Tatoeba Project (`https://tatoeba.org`) is an open, community-driven database of example sentences and cross-lingual translation pairs.
+
+### 1.1 Source Registration
+In NihongoBridge's authoritative provenance registry (`src/services/knowledge/provenance/registry.ts`), Tatoeba is registered with the following immutable parameters:
+- **ID**: `upstream:tatoeba:2024-07`
+- **Legacy Alias**: `tatoeba:corpus:2024-07`
+- **Domain**: `sentence`
+- **Type**: `upstream`
+- **Status**: `active`
+- **Target Table**: `example_sentences`
+- **Release Version**: `2024-07`
+- **Release Date**: `2024-07-01`
+- **URI**: `https://tatoeba.org`
+
+---
+
+## 2. Licensing & Attribution Contract
+
+All sentences in Tatoeba are contributed and published under the **Creative Commons Attribution 2.0 France (CC BY 2.0 FR)** license.
+
+### 2.1 Attribution Obligations
+To comply with Section 4(a) of CC BY 2.0 FR:
+1. **Mandatory Credit**: Every public display, API response, or export containing Tatoeba content must include the attribution string:
+   > *"Tatoeba Project (tatoeba.org) contributors under Creative Commons BY 2.0 FR."*
+2. **Upstream Linkage**: Every sentence retains its upstream Tatoeba sentence ID, enabling direct navigation to the canonical source entry:
+   `https://tatoeba.org/sentences/show/<sentenceId>`
+3. **Change Notation**: Text normalization applied to the raw export (such as Unicode NFKC and whitespace canonicalization) is explicitly documented.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Raw Artifact Integrity & Acquisition Verification
+
+1. **Local Storage**: Downloaded artifacts reside strictly within `/data/tatoeba/`, which is excluded from Git tracking via `.gitignore`.
+2. **Immutability**: Raw files (`sentences.tsv`, `links.tsv`, `tags.tsv`) are never modified in place. All parsing operates in read-only streaming mode.
+3. **Cryptographic Checksum**: Every acquisition artifact is verified against a SHA-256 hash before processing. If the hash deviates from `reports/gates/PHASE-14.5A-TATOEBA-ACQUISITION-MANIFEST.json`, the pipeline halts immediately (`ARTIFACT INTEGRITY MISMATCH`).
+
+---
+
+## 4. Normalization & Validation Contract
+
+- **Unicode NFKC**: Standardizes compatibility characters while preserving Japanese Kanji, Hiragana, Katakana, and punctuation.
+- **Control Character Scrubbing**: Safely eliminates ASCII control characters (0x00–0x1F, 0x7F) that pose injection or parsing hazards.
+- **Quality Taxonomy**:
+  - `valid`: Fully verified Japanese sentence with clean orthography and linked translation.
+  - `warning`: Linguistically acceptable sentence exhibiting pedagogical anomalies (e.g. length extremes, unlinked translation, duplicate text).
+  - `rejected`: Corrupted or non-Japanese record (e.g. invalid ID, empty text, non-`jpn` language tag).
+
+---
+
+## 5. Deterministic Identity & Linkage Architecture
+
+1. **Sentence Identity**:
+   ```ts
+   getTatoebaSentenceId(upstreamSentenceId) => "es-tat-" + upstreamSentenceId
+   ```
+2. **Relationship Preservation**:
+   - One Japanese sentence can link to multiple translation sentences (one-to-many).
+   - Multiple Japanese sentences can link to the same translation sentence (many-to-one).
+   - Relationships are preserved as structured arrays rather than flattened single strings.
+3. **Future Cross-Entity Linkage**:
+   - Sentences link dynamically to canonical `kanji_entries` via extracted kanji characters.
+   - Sentences link to `dictionary_entries` via deterministic keyword and substring matching (`SentenceMatcher`).
+   - Sentences link to `grammar_patterns` via rule-based structure matching.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Rollback & Reprocessing Protocol
+
+Because Phase 14.5A executes in pure dry-run mode with zero database writes:
+1. **Rollback**: Consists of deleting temporary acquisition files in `data/tatoeba/` and discarding dry-run reports.
+2. **Reprocessing**: Can be executed at any time; identical source artifacts and parser logic produce identical SHA-256 execution digests.
